    "result_text": "All 11 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` feature so that owners returned by the API include their name formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` (the generated DTO) with a `displayName` field during the build.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` from the stored names as `lastName + \", \" + firstName` (null-safe).\n\nBecause the create/get flow (`addOwner` \u2192 `getOwner`) both serialize the owner through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, the computed `displayName` is returned everywhere an owner is serialized \u2014 matching the spec's \"formatted exactly as 'LastName, FirstName' from the stored names.\"\n\n**Verification:** The full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 11, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 including the new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName`.",
